      "content": "but aromatherapy is just smells, right? like bread or flowers. what i mean is something deeper. like, could they actually use the HVAC system to disperse something more potent? like a fine mist of compounds that bypasses the senses and goes straight to the neurochemistry to trigger those specific cravings? it seems like a much more efficient way to control high-margin sales if they could actually pull it off.",
